        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-06 21:28:03.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20879 target: fix OUT double swab and xattr_list slot",
        "message": "LU-20879 target: fix OUT double swab and xattr_list slot\n\nout_handle() swabs each update buffer with\nlustre_swab_object_update_request(), which already swabs every\nobject_update in it, then swabs each update again with\nlustre_swab_object_update() while sizing the reply.  For a request\nfrom a peer of the other byte order, this puts ou_type,\nou_params_count and ou_result_size back into wire order, so the\nreply size and the walk to the next update are wrong, and the\nsecond pass walks a byte-swapped ou_params_count of params,\nswabbing memory past the end of the update.  Remove the second\nswab and make lustre_swab_object_update() static.\n\nout_xattr_list() gets its result buffer from reply slot 0 instead\nof the update's own reply index.  If OUT_XATTR_LIST is not the\nfirst update in a request, the xattr list overwrites the results\nof the earlier updates and is missing from its own result.  Use\nthe update's reply index, as out_xattr_get() does.  OSP sends\nOUT_XATTR_LIST alone in its request today, so this is latent.\n\nAlso print the real reply index in the out_attr_get() and\nout_index_lookup() debug messages.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 8abb5a19e437 (\"LU-3539 protocol: Change UPDATE_OBJ RPC format\")\nFixes: 4325b1e45664 (\"LU-4684 xattr: add list support for remote object\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I1a0d120aae182f672637633423b211c50f3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
